  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider titration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> solution versus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> oxalic acid solution. At the end point following burette readings were obtained.<br />(i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math><br />(ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math><br />(iii)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math><br />(iv) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math><br />(v) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math><br />If the volume of oxalic acid taken was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> then the molarity of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> solution is ___<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>. (Rounded-off to the nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi>NaOH</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi></math></p><p>eq. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>=</mo></math> eq. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p>or, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>or, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>68</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Nearest integer answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>.</p>",
